/target
crates/sdroxide-web/dist
crates/sdroxide-web/dist/index.html

# Vendoring rade_c put a CMakeLists.txt in the tree, so IDE CMake integrations
# (VS Code's CMake Tools) configure it on their own and leave a build tree and
# their own settings at the repo root. The real RADE build is driven by
# crates/sdroxide-rade/build.rs and lives under /target.
/build
/compile_commands.json
.cache/
.vscode/

# Building a vendored crate on its own — `cargo test --manifest-path
# vendor/<crate>/Cargo.toml`, which is how the patches in there are checked —
# leaves a target directory and a lock file of its own beside it. Neither is
# part of the vendored source: the workspace resolves those crates through
# `[patch.crates-io]` and its own `Cargo.lock`.
/vendor/*/target
/vendor/*/Cargo.lock

# AtCHAT / file-transfer received files (runtime output)
received/

# Release notes drafted for the GitHub release page, not part of the tree.
/RELEASE_NOTES*.md

# The operator/agent working notes — the live brief, the queue, the session
# history and the topic handovers. Kept on disk for the agent to work from,
# and out of the published tree (operator's instruction, 2026-10-28): they
# carry names, callsigns and station detail that do not belong in a public
# repo. `git add -A` would put them back, which is why they are named here.
# AGENTS.md and TODO.md are now published (previously kept local)
/docs/internal/
/docs/cquam-design.md
/docs/multi-window-brainstorm.md
/docs/skyroof-notes.md
/docs/swl-phase1-design.md
/docs/swl-phase2-3-design.md
/docs/synop-notes.md

# The running session handover, written for whoever picks this up next. Kept on
# disk and out of the tree.
/HANDOVER.md

# Python bytecode from the tools
__pycache__/
/out/
